From 3fe661e528ff977bcea17dd7e693069d60ab81c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nicholas DeTello <no-reply@detello.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 07:45:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] platform_profile: Recognize the kernel's
 "balanced-performance" spelling

The kernel's ACPI platform_profile class
(drivers/acpi/platform_profile.c) names
PLATFORM_PROFILE_BALANCED_PERFORMANCE "balanced-performance" (hyphen) in
/sys/firmware/acpi/platform_profile and platform_profile_choices.
acpi_platform_profile_value_to_profile() only matches
"balanced_performance" (underscore), so the hyphenated value is reported
as "Unhandled ACPI platform profile" and resolves to PPD_PROFILE_UNSET.
update_acpi_platform_profile_state() then drops the change, and ppd
keeps advertising whatever profile was active before, e.g. "performance"
after a firmware hotkey (acer-wmi's Predator mode key, among others) has
already switched the platform to balanced-performance.

The exact-match code came from commit 6b565b0b05a2 ("Recognize the
custom ACPI platform profile"), which replaced the previous first-letter
matching (under which "balanced-performance" mapped to balanced). Accept
the hyphenated kernel spelling and keep the underscore one for
compatibility.

Add an integration test that switches the sysfs attribute to
"balanced-performance" behind the daemon's back and expects
ActiveProfile to follow to "balanced".

Backported to 0.30 for the predator-nix bundle.

Fixes: 6b565b0b05a2 ("Recognize the custom ACPI platform profile")
(cherry picked from commit 16c0ad23a58aa57f0a8dd51045f6776831cbfc26)
---
 src/ppd-driver-platform-profile.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/ppd-driver-platform-profile.c b/src/ppd-driver-platform-profile.c
index 28fc33509..6a955b59b 100644
--- a/src/ppd-driver-platform-profile.c
+++ b/src/ppd-driver-platform-profile.c
@@ -89,6 +89,7 @@ acpi_platform_profile_value_to_profile (const char *str)
     return PPD_PROFILE_POWER_SAVER;
 
   if (g_str_equal (str, "balanced") ||
+      g_str_equal (str, "balanced-performance") ||
       g_str_equal (str, "balanced_performance") ||
       g_str_equal (str, "cool"))
     return PPD_PROFILE_BALANCED;
-- 
2.54.0

